Subject: A little function to clean corpus files, e.g. text files from the Project Gutenberg
Message-ID: <M0S3JNXkhvo.Ayo-B8-7AQAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/corpling-with-r/c/M0S3JNXkhvo/m/Ayo-B8-7AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi there,

I propose the following function to get rid of noise in text files such as texts from the Project Gutenberg. Any comments or suggestions are welcome!

#### This is a script to clean up corpus files from the Project Gutenberg ####

## Step 1: Load the corpus files into one vector of characters

## Step 2: Clean up the corpus files

clean.corpus.file<-function(x, lowercase=F, numbers=F, punctuation=F, spaces=T, noise=T) {

### a) x: a character string

### b) lowercase

if(lowercase) {
x<-tolower(x)
}

### c) numbers

if(numbers) {
x<-gsub("[[:digit:]]", "", x, perl=T)
}

### d) remove punctuation symbols

if(punctuation)
x<-gsub("[[:punct:]]", "", x, perl=T)

### e) remove extra white spaces

if(spaces) {
x<-gsub("[ \t]{2,}", " ", x, perl=T)
x<-gsub("^\\s+|\\s+$", "", x, perl=T)
}

### f) remove noise, i.e. characters that do not count as words, punctuation marks, etc.
if(noise) {
x<-gsub("(\\~*?|@*?|\\#*?|\\$*?|\\%*?|\\^*?|\\**?|\\{.*?\\}|_\\w*?|\\+*?|\\/|\\[.*?\\]|-.*?)", "", x, perl=T)
}

### g) return

x

}

