I realized how bad the function clean.corpus.file was written. Therefore, I publish an update of the function. I've tested it on my own corpus, and it works rather well. I paste it here.

clean.corpus.file<-function(x, lowercase=T, numbers=T, punctuation=T, spaces=T, noise=T) {

### a) x: character string

### b) lowercase

if(lowercase) {
x<-tolower(x)
}

### c) numbers

if(numbers) {
x<-gsub("[[:digit:]]", "", x, perl=T)
}

### d) remove punctuation symbols

if(punctuation)
x<-gsub("[[:punct:]]", "", x, perl=T)

### e) remove extra white spaces

if(spaces) {
x<-gsub("[ \t]{2,}", " ", x, perl=T)
x<-gsub("^\\s+|\\s+$", "", x, perl=T)
}

### f) remove noise, i.e. characters that do not count as words, punctuation marks, etc.

if(noise) {

x<-gsub("[#$%*<=>@^_`|~{}¿»«]", "", x, perl=T)
x<-gsub("\\[.*\\]", "", x, perl=T)
}

### g) return

x

}

Now I've got some trouble when it comes to output each cleaned text separately. Here is what I can manage to do:

rm(list=ls(all=T))

source(choose.files()) # for the function 'clean.corpus.file'

corpus.files<-choose.files()
whole.corpus<-vector()

for(i in 1:length(corpus.files)) {
  current.corpus.file<-scan(corpus.files[i], what="char", sep="\n", quiet=T)
  current.corpus.file.2<-clean.corpus.file(current.corpus.file, lowercase=F, numbers=F, punctuation=F)
  whole.corpus<-append(whole.corpus, current.corpus.file.2)
}

But then, when I want to save the output, I can't figure out how to do it separately for each text. Any ideas or suggestions?

